== Architecture ==
The architectural focus of this period was firstly on revivals and {{W|Eclecticism in architecture|eclecticism}}, and later on the creation of a "cosmopolitan" approach, drawing from across the confederation, and reflecting the [[Ethnography of Balisca|country's ethnography]]. 

The 1838 inauguration of [[Michelangelo Valentino]] and the new progressive [[Ani Federali|''Anyos Federales'']] also embraced this emerging "cosmopolitan style", and it rapidly rose in popularity. It is characterized by it's mix of decorative elements from various {{W|Old World}} styles, namely {{W|Neo-Mudéjar}}, {{W|Moorish Revival architecture|Moorish Revival}} and {{W|Palazzo style}}, and widespread use of {{W|Architectural terracotta|architectural ceramics}} and oriental motifs. The arrival of the arrival of new {{W|Modernisme}} to the Baliscan academic arena was relatively quick thanks to the emerging cultural and historical ties to the [[Mesogean world]], and heavily influenced the eventual development of [[New Cosmopolitan style]]. During the later years of the 20th century, there was a substantial interest in {{W|Moorish Revival architecture}}. 

